{%- comment -%}
  L'Oreal "Perfect Match" Mega Deal — configuration.

  Campaign mechanic (per L'Oreal Commercial & Technical Conditions):
    1 SKU from Collection 1 (Mega Deal SKUs) + 1 SKU from Collection 2
    (Perfect Match SKUs) in the same order unlocks a Mega Deal discount,
    applied to the Collection 1 SKU only. Max one deal per order, one per
    customer, and it must not stack with other discounts.

  Shopify enforces the money side: each tier below is a CODE-based Buy X Get Y
  discount (buy 1 from C2 -> 1 from C1 at N% off) with "one use per customer"
  and "does not combine". The theme only:
    - shows cart progress / unlocked state (kj-perfect-match.liquid)
    - applies the right tier code when the pair is present
      (assets/kj-perfect-match.js), so the shopper never types a code

  Tiers are per-percentage, because the approved C1 list prices SKUs at
  different discounts. Each tier lists the C1 product ids it covers.
  While `tiers` is empty the theme shows progress but applies nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign c1 = settings.kj_pm_collection_1
  assign c2 = settings.kj_pm_collection_2
-%}

{%- if settings.kj_pm_enabled and c1 != blank and c2 != blank -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="kj-perfect-match-rules">
  {
    "collection1": {{ c1.handle | json }},
    "collection2": {{ c2.handle | json }},
    "c1ProductIds": [
      {%- paginate c1.products by 250 -%}
        {%- for p in c1.products -%}{%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}{{ p.id }}{%- endfor -%}
      {%- endpaginate -%}
    ],
    "c2ProductIds": [
      {%- paginate c2.products by 250 -%}
        {%- for p in c2.products -%}{%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}{{ p.id }}{%- endfor -%}
      {%- endpaginate -%}
    ],
    "tiers": []
  }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
